{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_01a164050c2576178ff069fd38860fc4","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/agent/journal.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c4d1346-5ef5-4ae8-af7f-555535414d85","uuid":"07989c26-0305-4ec9-ade2-71a006ed47c5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:30:19.693Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/agent/journal.md","oldString":"- **Verdict**: keep v2 (current `modeling.py`). **Lesson**: remaining error is not in\n  drift/jumps/width — test conditional width per horizon bucket and microstructure (zero-step)\n  handling next; effects to chase are ≥0.2% or they drown in prompt noise.","newString":"- **Verdict**: keep v2 (current `modeling.py`). **Lesson**: remaining error is not in\n  drift/jumps/width — test conditional width per horizon bucket and microstructure (zero-step)\n  handling next; effects to chase are ≥0.2% or they drown in prompt noise.\n\n## Iteration 3 — PIT diagnostics + gap-return scaling\n- **Hypothesis**: per-horizon PIT (sd of realised/fan-sigma): 5m/30m/3h ≈ calibrated\n  (0.94–1.07 crypto, 0.6–0.99 equities), terminal fatter (1.25 BTC/SOL, tail exceedance\n  5–11% vs 1% Gaussian) — long-horizon vol-of-vol is under-dispersed. AAPLX's apparent\n  0.6 sd(z) over-width does NOT survive as a vol-level error: its gap-scaled returns are\n  identical to raw (measured gap lengths in scored weeks are 1–13 min only; the thin era\n  is not in the scored windows), so its over-width is intraday-shape, not level.\n  AC1 of realised 5m returns ≈ 0 (−0.06…+0.05): no exploitable mean reversion.\n- **Change**: gap-scaled returns (k-minute spans ÷√k, weight 1/k) in the EWMA — principled,\n  measured CRPS-neutral on the scored windows (v3 ≡ v2 to full precision).\n- **Verdict**: keep (harmless, correct for evaluation windows with longer gaps).\n  Next lever per PIT: raise long-horizon vol dispersion (slower vol mean-reversion /\n  larger volsd at long lags) without touching the calibrated 5m marginal.","originalFile":"# Journal — campaign-6\n\n## Iteration 0 — setup & scoring anatomy (pre-registered)\n- **Hypothesis**: Reading `synth.validator.crps_calculation`: 24h score = sum of CRPS over\n  return-changes at 5min (288 pts), 30min (48), 3h (8) + terminal absolute price (1, scaled).\n  1h score = return CRPS at 1/2/5/15/30min + terminal + 12 \"gap-from-start\" returns + vol-CRPS\n  (lambda=5.25 over 60/15/5min block realized-vol). So short-horizon marginals dominate counts,\n  and (for 1h) the *dispersion of block realized vol* is scored directly.\n- **Implication**: constant-vol Gaussian (starter) will be wrong on (a) time-of-day/week vol\n  seasonality, (b) vol clustering → block-RV dispersion & multi-horizon fat tails, (c) per-step\n  fat tails. Judge everything on CRPS via `agent/predict.py`, per config/asset.\n- **Plan**: EDA on snapshot → baseline starter CRPS → v1: EWMA vol level + per-asset seasonal\n  vol profile (fitted offline, embedded) + AR(1) log-vol + Student-t shocks, zero drift,\n  simulated at the scoring step. Kill thresholds set per experiment below.\n\n## Iteration 1 — EDA + v1 (seasonal SV Student-t fan)\n- **Hypothesis**: (a) vol seasonality is large (measured: equities/gold hour-of-day range\n  0.3–3.4x, weekend 0.2–0.6x of weekday; crypto flatter 0.5–2.1x, weekend 0.55–0.8x),\n  (b) 1-min standardized tails ≈ Student-t df 4–6 at 0.1% quantile, (c) vol clusters\n  (RV5m/RV1h variance ratio ≈ 0.75 → stochastic vol matters beyond per-step tails).\n- **Change**: `modeling.py` v1 — deseasonalised returns via per-asset (weekday×hour) profile\n  fitted offline (`artifacts.json`); level = 0.7·fast(6h HL)+0.3·slow(3d HL) EWMA variance;\n  forward AR(1) log-vol (6h half-life, stationary sd 0.45 in log-sigma), t(6) shocks,\n  re-seasonalised, simulated at 1-min, sub-sampled to the scoring step. Env-switchable\n  NU/VOLSD/FASTW/SEAS/SV for ablation. Seed: `SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED` + asset|start_time CRC.\n- **Result** (3d to 2026-09-30, 1000 paths, official backtester; starter → v1):\n  BTC 24h 2329.4 → **2185.9** (−6.2%); XAU 24h 1383.0 → **1147.6** (−17.0%);\n  BTC 1h (--latest-formula) 539.1 → **509.6** (−5.5%).\n- **Verdict**: keep v1 as new base. **Lesson**: seasonality is the big lever for COM_EQU;\n  ablate before tuning further.\n\n## Iteration 2 — ablations, event study, v2 tuning\n- **Ablations** (2d, BTC/XAU): no-seasonality +26.8%/+6.1% CRPS worse; no-SV +0.9%/+0.9%\n  worse. Seasonality is the dominant term; SV is small but consistent.\n- **Fast proxy** (custom CRPS replicating validator intervals; verified vs properscoring):\n  drift (0.5–1.0× trailing mean) HURTS (+2–7%), jump mixture HURTS, seasonal exponent\n  ±20% neutral, nu 4–8 flat, volsd 0.2–0.35 slightly better than 0.45, fastw 0.85 best.\n  Wedge: fast proxy overstated gains vs official (300 paths, log-approx) — only use for sign.\n- **Windows**: the offline bundle only has scored prompts ~2026-09-07→10-11, so the second\n  validation window is eval-end 2026-10-11 (not August). Field study: bundle-wide best-miner\n  mean CRPS sits ~1.5–2% below the median miner on every asset — the field is tightly packed.\n- **Event study** (deseasonalised |r| pooled, 2h post-event vol ratio): CPI ×1.47 (crypto)/\n  ×1.26 (equity), FOMC ×1.9/×1.35 — strong; NFP/GDP/PCE/PPI ×1.15–1.2 — mild; EIA, earnings,\n  retail ≈ 1.0 — none. Added decaying multipliers (CPI 1.45, FOMC 1.8, others 1.15–1.2, 60-min\n  half-life) to `modeling.py`, read from `$SYNTH_BENCHMARK_CALENDAR` at serve time.\n- **v2 result** (nu 6→5, volsd 0.45→0.35, fastw 0.7→0.85, +events): 24h −0.12%, 1h −0.07%\n  mean across 30 asset-window cells, 24/30 improved, both windows same sign.\n- **Verdict**: keep v2 (current `modeling.py`). **Lesson**: remaining error is not in\n  drift/jumps/width — test conditional width per horizon bucket and microstructure (zero-step)\n  handling next; effects to chase are ≥0.2% or they drown in prompt noise.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":48,"oldLines":3,"newStart":48,"newLines":17,"lines":[" - **Verdict**: keep v2 (current `modeling.py`). **Lesson**: remaining error is not in","   drift/jumps/width — test conditional width per horizon bucket and microstructure (zero-step)","   handling next; effects to chase are ≥0.2% or they drown in prompt noise.","+","+## Iteration 3 — PIT diagnostics + gap-return scaling","+- **Hypothesis**: per-horizon PIT (sd of realised/fan-sigma): 5m/30m/3h ≈ calibrated","+  (0.94–1.07 crypto, 0.6–0.99 equities), terminal fatter (1.25 BTC/SOL, tail exceedance","+  5–11% vs 1% Gaussian) — long-horizon vol-of-vol is under-dispersed. AAPLX's apparent","+  0.6 sd(z) over-width does NOT survive as a vol-level error: its gap-scaled returns are","+  identical to raw (measured gap lengths in scored weeks are 1–13 min only; the thin era","+  is not in the scored windows), so its over-width is intraday-shape, not level.","+  AC1 of realised 5m returns ≈ 0 (−0.06…+0.05): no exploitable mean reversion.","+- **Change**: gap-scaled returns (k-minute spans ÷√k, weight 1/k) in the EWMA — principled,","+  measured CRPS-neutral on the scored windows (v3 ≡ v2 to full precision).","+- **Verdict**: keep (harmless, correct for evaluation windows with longer gaps).","+  Next lever per PIT: raise long-horizon vol dispersion (slower vol mean-reversion /","+  larger volsd at long lags) without touching the calibrated 5m marginal."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_50d485dd-a5fb-4aab-b075-861b9c1a4fc3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_01a1640526577493994f83395b9e2f69","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/agent/fast_eval4.py","content":"\"\"\"Screen vol mean-reversion speed x volsd on the fast proxy (24h), BTC/SOL/XAU.\"\"\"\nimport sys, warnings, os\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\nsys.path.insert(0, \"agent\")\nimport numpy as np, pandas as pd, json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions import load_minute_prices\n\nWS = Path(\".\").resolve()\nART = json.loads(Path(\"agent/artifacts.json\").read_text())\n\ndef crps_ens(obs, ens):\n    ens = np.sort(ens); n = len(ens)\n    return float(np.mean(np.abs(ens - obs)) - np.sum((2*np.arange(1, n+1) - n - 1) * ens) / (n*n))\n\ndef run(asset, close, nu=5, volsd=0.35, fastw=0.85, phi_hl=360, n_paths=300, seed=7):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    prof = np.asarray(ART[asset][\"profile\"])\n    idx = close.index; p = close.values.astype(float)\n    ok = np.isfinite(p) & (p > 0)\n    lp = np.where(ok, np.log(np.where(ok, p, 1.0)), np.nan)\n    r_all = np.diff(lp); H = 1440\n    phi = 0.5 ** (1/phi_hl)\n    total = 0.0; cnt = 0\n    for st in pd.date_range(\"2026-09-02\", \"2026-09-28\", freq=\"12h\", tz=\"UTC\"):\n        i = {t: k for k, t in enumerate(idx)}.get(st)\n        if i is None or i < 7*1440 or i + H >= len(p): continue\n        ctx_r = r_all[i-7*1440:i]; ci = idx[i-7*1440:i]\n        u = ctx_r / prof[ci.weekday, ci.hour]; u = u[np.isfinite(u)]\n        cap = np.quantile(np.abs(u), 0.999); uc = np.clip(u, -cap, cap)\n        sq = pd.Series(uc*uc)\n        fast = max(float(sq.ewm(halflife=360, adjust=False).mean().iloc[-1]), 1e-12)\n        slow = max(float(sq.ewm(halflife=4320, adjust=False).mean().iloc[-1]), 1e-12)\n        mu = 0.5*np.log(slow); start = mu + fastw*(0.5*np.log(fast)-mu)\n        fut = idx[i:i+H]; seas_f = prof[fut.weekday, fut.hour]\n        log_sig = np.full(n_paths, start); eps_sd = volsd*np.sqrt(1-phi*phi)\n        rets = np.empty((n_paths, H))\n        for j in range(H):\n            rets[:, j] = np.exp(log_sig)*seas_f[j]*(rng.standard_t(nu, size=n_paths)/np.sqrt(nu/(nu-2)))\n            log_sig = mu + phi*(log_sig-mu) + eps_sd*rng.standard_normal(n_paths)\n        rc = np.concatenate([[0.0], np.cumsum(np.nan_to_num(r_all[i:i+H]))])\n        sim_cum = np.concatenate([np.zeros((n_paths,1)), np.cumsum(rets, axis=1)], axis=1)\n        s5s, s5r = sim_cum[:, ::5], rc[::5]\n        raw = r_all[i:i+H]\n        for k in [1, 6, 36]:\n            sim_ch = (s5s[:, k:] - s5s[:, :-k])*1e4; real_ch = (s5r[k:] - s5r[:-k])*1e4\n            for t in range(sim_ch.shape[1]):\n                if np.isfinite(raw[t*5:(t+k)*5]).all():\n                    total += crps_ens(real_ch[t], sim_ch[:, t]); cnt += 1\n        total += crps_ens(rc[-1]*1e4, sim_cum[:, -1]*1e4); cnt += 1\n    return total/max(cnt,1)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    for asset in [\"BTC\", \"SOL\", \"XAU\"]:\n        close = load_minute_prices(WS/\"market_data\", asset, pd.Timestamp(\"2026-08-20\", tz=\"UTC\"),\n                                   pd.Timestamp(\"2026-09-29\", tz=\"UTC\"))[\"close\"]\n        for name, kw in [(\"hl360 sd.35\", {}), (\"hl720 sd.35\", {\"phi_hl\":720}), (\"hl720 sd.5\", {\"phi_hl\":720,\"volsd\":0.5}),\n                         (\"hl1440 sd.5\", {\"phi_hl\":1440,\"volsd\":0.5}), (\"hl1440 sd.65\", {\"phi_hl\":1440,\"volsd\":0.65}),\n                         (\"hl360 sd.5\", {\"volsd\":0.5}), (\"hl2880 sd.5\", {\"phi_hl\":2880,\"volsd\":0.5})]:\n            print(asset, name, round(run(asset, close, **kw), 3), flush=True)\n"}}],"model":"meta/muse-wonder-1.0","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c4d1346-5ef5-4ae8-af7f-55553